# =============================================================================
# Forge-OH .gitignore — governed by ADR-016 (Colossus ↔ GitHub mirror parity)
# =============================================================================
# Every rule below has an explicit reason. If you remove a rule, the path it
# matched will start showing up in `git status` and must be either tracked or
# get a new ignore rule with its own justification.
#
# Never add an ignore rule without a comment explaining why.
# =============================================================================

# --- Local env files (contain API keys, DB passwords) ------------------------
# Sensitive. Never track. Templates live at .env.example / .env.local.example.
.env
.env.local
.env.development.local
.env.test.local
.env.production.local
.env.neo4j
# Committed templates:
!.env.example
!.env.local.example
!.env.test

# --- Auth artifacts ----------------------------------------------------------
# Session tokens, private keys, browser auth state.
.auth/
*.pem

# --- Runtime databases -------------------------------------------------------
# User conversations, preset state, run history. May contain accidentally-typed
# secrets. Regenerable via seed data.
bff/data/
data/

# --- Python venvs ------------------------------------------------------------
# Regenerable from requirements.txt. Machine-specific paths, huge.
.oh-venv/
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.egg-info/

# --- Node / Next build artifacts ---------------------------------------------
# All regenerable. Never source of truth.
node_modules/
.pnp
.pnp.js
.next/
out/
build/
dist/
next-env.d.ts
*.tsbuildinfo
package-lock.json

# --- Runtime logs (may contain prompt/response text) -------------------------
# Forge-OH runtime writes agent-server.log, bff.log, frontend.log here. These
# logs contain user prompt text and model responses — potentially sensitive.
# Recreated on every `forge-up.sh` run.
.forge-logs/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
playwright-next-debug.log

# --- Bench outputs (per forge-oh-bench-methodology skill) --------------------
# Bench artifacts stay local. Only ADR verdicts + harness scripts commit.
# ~/.forge-oh/bench_* lives outside the repo, but the sibling .forge-oh/ inside
# the repo holds sidecar trajectory state and verify-state.json.
.forge-oh/

# --- Runtime scratch: agent workspaces, test outputs, screenshots ------------
# `workspaces/` (plural) is created by selfeval smoke runs.
# `workspace/` (singular) is the legacy single-workspace path.
# `worktrees/` for git worktrees.
workspace/
workspaces/
worktrees/
/coverage
coverage/
.coverage
/test-results
test-results/
/playwright-report
playwright-report/
/blob-report
blob-report/
screenshots/
playwright-artifacts/

# --- Storybook -------------------------------------------------------------
storybook-static/

# --- Backups + local machine noise -------------------------------------------
.ai-backups/
*.bak
.DS_Store
.vercel

# =============================================================================
# NOTE: The following rules were REMOVED in ADR-016 (2026-08-05):
#   tests/    — directory does not exist on Colossus; tests/ belongs on GitHub per ADR-016
#   scripts/  — was force-tracked; ignore rule was dead and misleading
# If you re-introduce either as a working directory, add an explicit rule with rationale.
# =============================================================================
